WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.590
For Us, the highly anticipated follow-up to
his smash hit directorial debut Get Out, filmmaker

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:10.530
Jordan Peele assembled an A-list ensemble
filled with familiar faces, as well as one

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:11.540
or two surprises.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:15.980
Here's why you feel like you've seen the cast
of Us before and where you saw them first.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.960
Lupita Nyong'o is among the most pedigreed
members of the Us cast after modest beginnings

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:26.780
as a production assistant, she earned a master's
degree in drama from Yale University, and

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.750
booked her first major film role shortly after
graduation.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.360
Nyong'o's work in Steve McQueen's 12 Years
A Slave netted the young talent her first

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:38.160
Oscar for Best Supporting Actress, making
her a breakout star.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.800
"500 pounds of cotton, day in, day out!"

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.900
After big moves like joining the Star Wars
universe, Nyong'o joined the cast of Black

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.720
Panther, a Marvel juggernaut that crushed
box office records and won multiple Oscars.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:58.880
As Nakia, a Wakandan spy who was also a love
interest for King T'challa, Nyong'o proved

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:03.309
she could headline a blockbuster as well as
perform in a prestige drama, making her mark

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:05.640
as one of the most versatile stars around.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:11.990
Born in Tobago and raised in upstate New York,
Winston Duke pursued an acting M.F.A. at Yale

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:15.800
University, where he met his classmate and
future co-star Lupita Nyong'o.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:21.840
After earning his degree, Duke booked a seven-episode
arc as the violent criminal Dominic on CBS'

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:22.600
Person of Interest.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:27.280
Duke racked up several TV appearances in the
years since, but most people recognize Duke

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.980
from his breakout role in Black Panther as
M'Baku, who leads Wakanda's mountain tribe.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.780
Tim Heidecker's name might not be immediately
recognizable if you don't watch a lot of late

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:42.690
night cable TV, but once you pair him with
his comedy partner Eric Wareheim, it might

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:43.460
jog your memory.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:48.719
The duo's show, Tim and Eric Awesome Show,
Great Job!, ran on Adult Swim from 2007 to

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:49.440
2010.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:53.369
"I go up and I look at the stars through my
telescope and I see the Little Dipster, or

00:01:53.369 --> 00:01:54.400
I see the Big Dipster."

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:59.680
Heidecker has appeared in a few films, including
Bridesmaids and Marvel's Ant-Man and the Wasp,

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.000
and is typically cast for the offbeat, irreverent
sense of humor that informs nearly all of

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.000
his work with Wareheim and his other comedic
collaborators.

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:11.860
But his disturbing turn as an emotionally
stunted hipster in 2012's The Comedy showed

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.740
he's also right at home in horror …

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:15.880
"You can't f----- stab me.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.420
You can't f----- stab me."

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:24.700
Known for her award-winning roles in some
of television's best prestige dramas, Elisabeth

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:29.860
Moss is a veteran of TV and film who regularly
delivers incredible performances, regardless

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:30.480
of the medium.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:35.000
Moss got her start in television on Aaron
Sorkin's popular drama The West Wing, before

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.940
going on to appear in major films like Girl,
Interrupted.

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:42.800
Her breakthrough came in Mad Men, the AMC
advertising firm drama now hailed as one of

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:48.110
the best series of all time, in which Moss
played Peggy Olson, an initially meek secretary

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:51.880
who ends the series as an advertising executive
with her own office.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:56.880
Her first Emmy win came for her work in Hulu's
The Handmaid's Tale, an adaptation of Margaret

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.870
Atwood's seminal dystopian novel.

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:04.790
The Wilson children in Us, Zora and Jason,
are played by Shahadi Wright Joseph and Evan

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:06.000
Alex, respectively.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:10.960
Joseph, who plays the older sister, has primarily
worked on the stage, appearing in School of

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:14.960
Rock on Broadway and on television in 2016's
Hairspray Live!.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:19.300
Us marks her first feature film credit, for
which she has already earned praise.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:23.500
Alex, the younger sibling, has appeared on
television shows like Jim Carrey's Kidding

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:27.820
as well as several episodes of the YouTube
series Mani, and is also earning his first

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:28.880
film credit in Us.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:35.720
Anna Diop got her television start in 2006
with a recurring role on Everybody Hates Chris,

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:38.060
setting the stage for a busy career to come.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:42.720
Diop got her first major television role as
a series regular on the CW's The Messengers,

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:47.360
a show about five strangers who suddenly find
themselves with supernatural abilities.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:52.640
After appearing on two episodes on Quantico,
Diop booked a main role in 24: Legacy, a sequel

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.140
to the popular Fox drama.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:58.960
She currently stars in the DC web series Titans
as Starfire, one of the core members of the

00:03:58.960 --> 00:03:59.740
super-team.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:05.560
Despite her young age and relatively small
resume, Kara Hayward has already made an impressive

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:10.770
entry into arthouse films at just 14, she
landed a starring role in Wes Anderson's whimsical

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:11.920
Moonrise Kingdom.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.910
Hayward received plenty of praise for her
breakout performance, in which she held their

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:20.900
own against several Oscar-winning actors,
many of whom were frequent Anderson collaborators.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:25.380
If you're a big fan of YouTube personality
Miranda Sings, you may have also seen Hayward

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:30.230
in Season 2 of Haters Back Off, the Netflix
original comedy series based on the popular

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:31.230
YouTube channel.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.960
Yet another Us cast member with a master's
degree from the Yale School of Drama, Yahya

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:42.940
Abdul-Mateen burst onto the scene in 2016
with a huge role on The Get Down, a Netflix

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:46.440
series about disco and hip-hop in New York
in the 1970s.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:50.600
The show was canceled after its first season,
freeing up Abdul-Mateen to appear in some

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:55.660
major feature films, including a role as a
police officer in the film adaptation of Baywatch.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:05:00.780
After appearing in DC Comics' Aquaman as Black
Manta, one of the film's two villains, it

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:03.160
was announced that Abdul-Mateen would appear
in Us.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:07.260
It looks like Jordan Peele took a liking to
Abdul-Mateen, as the actor is also set to

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.360
play the lead in the Peele-produced Candyman.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:15.120
They're still teens, but identical twins Cali
&amp; Noelle Sheldon have a handful of acting

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:19.350
credits to their name, including in one of
the most popular sitcoms of all time.

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:24.410
As infants, the twins appeared on Friends
as Emma, Rachel and Ross' baby, for a total

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:25.620
of eight episodes.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:30.940
At 16, the twins were cast in Us as Gwen and
Maggie Tyler, carrying on a long tradition

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:34.930
of twins in horror, perhaps most notably in
Stanley Kubrick's The Shining.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:35.980
Sorry, twins.

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:36.800
You're kinda creepy.

